From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:55:47 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/32] Manage: pass force and verbose to Manage_remove() in
 their order

Manage_remove() takes force before verbose, but Manage_subdevs() has
passed them the other way round since force was added to it.  So
hot_remove_disk() and sys_hot_remove_disk() get the verbose level as
force, and Manage_remove() gets --force as the verbose level:

- --remove --force waits only 50 ms for a busy device to be released,
  not the 5 s it should;
- --remove with --quiet or --verbose waits up to 5 s for it;
- "hot removed ..." is printed with --quiet too.

Pass them in the order of the prototype.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.

Fixes: 1ab9ed2afb7c ("Add 'force' flag to *hot_remove_disk().")
---
 Manage.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Manage.c b/Manage.c
index 53eb1239..83ce1e1d 100644
--- a/Manage.c
+++ b/Manage.c
@@ -1656,7 +1656,7 @@ int Manage_subdevs(char *devname, int fd,
 				pr_err("Cannot remove disks from a \'member\' array, perform this operation on the parent container\n");
 				rv = -1;
 			} else
-				rv = Manage_remove(tst, fd, dv, sysfd, rdev, verbose, force,
+				rv = Manage_remove(tst, fd, dv, sysfd, rdev, force, verbose,
 						   devname);
 			close_fd(&sysfd);
 

